# Rod and sword fishing end to end (docs/design/fish-and-fishing.md Phase D,
# 4.1 to 4.6). The player stands on the shore of seed 12345 at 6.5 15.5, found
# by scanning for dry land with four blocks of water to its east, with a fish
# spawned one cell below the feet two blocks east. A player in the water would
# scatter the fish and drop its lure. The bite delay is seeded, so
# `until` finds the dip on the same frame every run.

case the rod casts, bites, reels in the window and puts a raw fish in the hands
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
held tool:fishing_rod
face fish
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50
expect event line_cast
until bobber = floating
until bobber = dipping
expect event fish_bite
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50 x2
expect event fish_caught method=rod
expect event line_reeled
expect bobber = none
expect hands != none
expect fish = 0

case a bite splashes and the particles are gone once the burst is over
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
held tool:fishing_rod
face fish
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50
until bobber = dipping
expect event fish_bite
expect particles > 0
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50 x2
expect event fish_caught method=rod
frame 50 x40
expect particles = 0

case a lured fish leaves a wake before it bites
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
held tool:fishing_rod
face fish
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50
until bobber = floating
expect particles = 0
until particles > 0
expect bobber = floating
expect no event fish_bite

case with the day's stock gone a floating bobber beside a fish never bites
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
stock 0
held tool:fishing_rod
face fish
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50
until bobber = floating
# 400 ticks, well past the longest bite delay (160, data/fishing.toml)
frame 50 x400
expect bobber = floating
expect no event fish_bite
expect fish = 1

case a press outside the window catches nothing
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
held tool:fishing_rod
face fish
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50
until bobber = floating
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50 x2
expect event line_reeled
expect no event fish_bite
expect no event fish_caught
expect bobber = none
expect hands = none
expect fish = 1

case casting while carrying does nothing
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
held item:seeds
mouse 0 200
button down right
frame 50
button up right
frame 50 x2
expect no event line_cast
expect bobber = none

case a sword hit on a fish gives its raw item and leaves one fewer
start walk stream at 6.5 15.5
click
lock
frame 50 x40
spawn fish salmon -1
expect fish = 1
held tool:sword
face fish
frame 50 x2
expect target.kind = entity
expect rule.primary = attack
button down left
frame 50
button up left
frame 50 x2
expect fish = 0
expect hands != none
expect event fish_caught method=sword
